                        "content": "The nurse is reviewing the history of a client with bladder cancer. The nurse expects to note documentation of which most common sign or symptom of this type of cancer?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nThe most common sign in clients with cancer of the bladder is hematuria. The client also may experience irritative voiding symptoms such as frequency, urgency, and dysuria, and these symptoms often are associated with carcinoma in situ. Dysuria, urgency, and frequency of urination are also symptoms of a bladder infection.",
                        "id": "7a88b73e5c05486990504edec23eda09",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "19ef8529498e4fe091809cba002a4bad",
                                "content": "Rupture of the bladder"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "b8a6755e281c4f1a9066eb8f63787dc5",
                                "content": "The development of a vesicovaginal fistula"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "b88702d430f84570a3564d2e37e6d4ac",
                                "content": "Extreme stress caused by the diagnosis of cancer"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "7bda4be73d744b938b127da94665b102",
                                "content": "Altered perineal sensation as a side effect of radiation therapy"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "19ef8529498e4fe091809cba002a4bad",
                                    "content": "Rupture of the bladder"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "b8a6755e281c4f1a9066eb8f63787dc5",
                                    "content": "The development of a vesicovaginal fistula"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "b88702d430f84570a3564d2e37e6d4ac",
                                    "content": "Extreme stress caused by the diagnosis of cancer"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "7bda4be73d744b938b127da94665b102",
                                    "content": "Altered perineal sensation as a side effect of radiation therapy"
                                }
                            ]
                        },
