                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "A client is receiving intravesical chemotherapy for cancer of the bladder. The nurse would plan to take which action after the completion of each treatment?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "80db17ea97ed8fdcd1b6b9666390fca1",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Applying 应用",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nAfter intravesical chemotherapy, the nurse increases fluids to help flush the medication out of the bladder after the period of retention. The client does not have a need for opioid analgesics as a result of the chemotherapy treatment, nor does the client need to be NPO. The chemotherapy agent and the urine are treated as biohazards, but the client does not need to be placed on contact isolation.",
                        "id": "b8fdb791f9a34138b9120d42176d6e86",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "1e6ab3fb6bef4b73a0863628030e8f1b",
                                "content": "Dietary restrictions"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "6534d1f8f8dc46e28e2d3a288b494666",
                                "content": "Technique of catheterization"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "a34da71d526241e087b7aafe2518cb14",
                                "content": "External pouch and application care"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "c251ebc8b80948c281704bedb0926419",
                                "content": "Proper administration of prophylactic antibiotics"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "1e6ab3fb6bef4b73a0863628030e8f1b",
                                    "content": "Dietary restrictions"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "6534d1f8f8dc46e28e2d3a288b494666",
                                    "content": "Technique of catheterization"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "a34da71d526241e087b7aafe2518cb14",
                                    "content": "External pouch and application care"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "c251ebc8b80948c281704bedb0926419",
                                    "content": "Proper administration of prophylactic antibiotics"
                                }
                            ]
                        },
                        "isSubmit": "0",
